.el .ds Aq '
.TH elfshaker-list 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-list \- List snapshots in known pack indexes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker list\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPACK\fR]... 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists snapshots from every known pack index, or only from the selected packs when PACK is supplied. Output lines are sorted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: %s]
Pretty\-print each result using placeholders:
	%s \- fully\-qualified snapshot
	%t \- snapshot tag
	%h \- human\-readable size
	%b \- size in bytes
	%n \- number of files

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPACK\fR]...
Pack index to list; may be repeated.
